Upstream gap: Open WebUI sends chat documents to models only as extracted text
or through its file tools, never as files, sends chat images only inline as
data URLs, and has no content extraction engine that reads text from an
OpenAI-compatible Files API. Upstream closed both native file input PRs
unmerged:

https://github.com/open-webui/open-webui/pull/27627
https://github.com/open-webui/open-webui/pull/27998

A model whose ID, or whose workspace base model ID, matches
OPENAI_FILES_API_MODELS_REGEX_PATTERN receives each user message's documents
with an OPENAI_FILES_API_FILE_EXTENSIONS extension as standard Chat file parts
with their Files API file_id, which Responses connections send as input_file.
Each stored raster image a user message shows becomes, in place of its
image_url part, an input_image part with its Files API file_id and detail.
Chat Completions has no such part, so a matching model must read Responses
parts, as a Responses connection or a Pipe that calls the Responses API does.
The request's files lists drop the files sent by ID, as for a Filter's
file_handler, so retrieval, the builtin file tools, and the attached files
context skip them. Audio, video, other files, and files whose upload fails
keep Open WebUI's usual handling.

CONTENT_EXTRACTION_ENGINE=openai_files sends processed uploads with an
OPENAI_FILES_API_FILE_EXTENSIONS extension to the Files API, as upstream's
MINERU_FILE_EXTENSIONS does for its mineru engine; other files keep the
built-in loaders. Loader.aload uploads the processing's local copy, waits
with the OpenAI SDK's wait_for_processing, and reads files-api's extracted
content JSON from GET /files/{file_id}/content by its type: a text file's text,
a spreadsheet's row chunks, or, untyped, a parsed document's markdown results.
Another type fails the processing until this patch reads it. Loader.load then
returns that text through _get_loader, post-processed as for every engine.

Both need OPENAI_FILES_API_BASE_URL. A pattern without it turns file IDs off
with an error at startup, as an invalid pattern does; the engine, which can
change at runtime, fails each upload it would send instead.

Open WebUI uploads a file on first use with purpose=user_data and keeps its ID
in the file's meta as openai_file_id. Requests go through the OpenAI SDK,
authenticate like the OpenAI connection with the same base URL
(get_connection_api_key from speech-images-system-oauth.patch), send
OPENAI_FILES_API_PARAMS as query parameters, and time out after
OPENAI_FILES_API_TIMEOUT seconds, which also bounds the wait for processing.
Files are never deleted from the Files API.

Removal check: an Open WebUI release that sends chat documents and images by
Files API file ID and extracts document text through a Files API.

